@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Storage outage and retry
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
participant "AddResourcesHandler" as h
participant "ResourceMaintenanceWorker" as w
participant "ResourceStorageRetryHandler" as r
participant "AzureBlobFileStorage" as store
database "Community database" as db
actor "Signed-in member" as member
h -> store : SaveAsync(blob)
store --> h : Fails (storage unavailable)
h -> h : File.MarkStoring(); ResourceBlobTask.Save(resourceId, blobName, bytes, contentType, now)
h -> db : Save Resource and task together (L2-057 AC11)
member -> h : (via API) list and open the resource
note right of member
  Listed with its type icon; the download answers
  409 "This file is still uploading. Try again in a minute."
end note
loop every outbox interval
  w -> r : RetryDueAsync()
  r -> db : Tasks with NextAttemptAt <= now
  alt Save
    r -> store : SaveAsync(blobName, content)
    alt succeeds
      r -> r : File.MarkStored(); remove the task
    else fails again
      r -> r : task.Failed(now): backoff doubling, at most one hour
    end
  else Delete
    r -> store : DeleteAsync(blobName)
    r -> r : Remove the task on success, else Failed(now)
  end
  r -> db : Save
end
member -> h : Download again
note right of member: 200 with the original file name, no new upload needed
@enduml
